  <iati-identifier>GB-CHC-202918-BGDD20</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-202918" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam GB</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Disasters Resilience Capacity of the Monsoon Flood Affected Population</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A series of interventions have been designed such as local infrastructures development through cash for work prior disaster, establishing resilient livelihood option, resilient Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) facilities, Disaster Management Committees (DMCs) capacity building, training on alternative Income Generating Activities (IGA), establish food and fodder banks, establish, Resilient Water Facilities (Double Platform Tube well), establish high raised sanitation facilities (Twin Offset Pit Pour Flash Latrine), WASH/Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR)/Waterborne Disease Prevention Training for community capacity building, vulnerable household profiling and digitalization, Joint Action Planning (JAP),  support to government for activating Ward Disaster Management Committees to implement Standing Orders of Disasters (SOD), Contingency Planning, emergency stock piling (contingency stoking) at community level to reduce the loss and damage of the communities in future disasters.</narrative>
  </description>
